hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1221","Ali ibn Hajar al-Saadi, our Ismail, meaning Ibn Jafar, told us Muhammad, who is Ibn Abi Harmala, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yasar, on the authority of Abu Dharr said: “My friend advised me to do three things that I will never give up, God willing, ever. He advised me to pray the forenoon prayer, to perform the witr prayer before going to sleep, and to fast.” Three days of every month.”"
"1222","Bishr bin Khaled Al-Askari told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: “My friend advised me to do three things: to fast three days of every month, and not to sleep except to pray the Witr prayer, and to perform the two rak’ahs of Duha.”"
